alf visible in the sky.\n4. Waxing gibbous: The moon continues to appear larger and fuller as it approaches full moon.\n5. Full moon: The entire face of the moon is illuminated by the sun.\n6. Waning gibbous: The moon appears to be decreasing in size as it moves away from full moon.\n7. Last quarter: The left half of the moon is illuminated, with the right half in shadow.\n8. Waning crescent: The moon appears as a thin crescent in the eastern sky.", "new_cot_probs": [0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0], "cot_prob": [-0.3657517433166504], "cot_step_prob": [-0.34143728017807007]}, "4": {"completion": "B): alter the way the moon's facade looks", "probs": [0.0023758902680128813, 0.9585025310516357, 0.015492750331759453, 0.022541819140315056], "prediction": 1, "target_cot_step": "Waxing Crescent: The moon appears to be growing larger as more of its illuminated surface is visible from Earth.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Moon phases\n\nChoices:\n(A): change the moon into cheese\n(B): alter the way the moon's facade looks\n(C): change moon lakes into vapor\n(D): cause lunar eclipse every day\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\nMoon phases refer to the different shapes and appearances of the moon as it orbits around the Earth.\nThe moon's appearance changes as it moves through different positions relative to the Earth and the sun.\nThe phases include:\n1.\nNew Moon: The side of the moon facing the Earth is not illuminated by the sun.\n2.", "specificity_preds": [2, 3, 0, 2, 3, 1, 3, 3, 2, 1, 2, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0, 3], "specificity_probs": [[5.810186848975718e-05, 5.1274721045047045e-05, 0.9966927766799927, 0.003172254888340831], [0.08542761206626892, 0.011561369523406029, 0.18085025250911713, 0.7152765989303589], [0.7381527423858643, 0.004389216657727957, 0.23964311182498932, 0.017359688878059387], [0.00035960384411737323, 0.0001322908647125587, 0.9460048079490662, 0.05336994305253029], [0.00020322368072811514, 0.00015827076276764274, 0.0008037652587518096, 0.9987